  "final_message": "I've built the base64 converter: a Flask API in `backend/app.py` and a React + Tailwind frontend in `frontend/src/`. I tested the API end to end under gunicorn and it behaves as specified. The frontend type-checks and builds, but I haven't clicked through it in a browser (none was available). I also couldn't build the Docker image because Docker isn't installed here, so the `Dockerfile` hasn't been tested.\n\n**What the API test run showed:**\n- Encoding and decoding work, including accented characters, emoji and empty text.\n- Invalid base64 gets a 400 with a readable message (bad padding, characters outside the alphabet, or output that isn't UTF-8 text). The frontend shows that message.\n- Registering answers 201 and a taken username gets 409. Login returns a token, and requests without a valid token get 401.\n- One user can't see or delete another user's conversions; they get 404.\n- History comes back newest first with paging. `page_size` is capped at 100.\n- Accounts survive a restart: I registered, restarted the server, and logged in again. The database is `data/app.db`.\n\n**Things I added that you didn't ask for:**\n- Endpoints: `POST /api/auth/logout`, `GET /api/auth/me` and `GET /api/conversions/{id}`.\n- Fields: login also returns `username`, and each conversion also includes `input_length` and `output_length`.\n- Previews are cut to 100 characters, and request bodies are limited to 2 MB.\n- Passwords are stored hashed, and only a hash of each sign-in token is stored. Tokens expire after 30 days.\n\n**Frontend:** it has sign-in and registration tabs, the username with a sign-out button, the two text areas with Encode, Decode and Copy buttons, and the API's error messages. Signed-in users also get the \"Save to history\" switch and the history list with delete buttons and paging. The browser keeps the sign-in token in `localStorage`.\n\n**Dependencies:** I added Tailwind v4 (through its Vite plugin), TypeScript and the React type packages as dev dependencies, pinned in `package.json` and `package-lock.json`. There's a new `npm run typecheck` script. I also added a `.gitignore`, and a local `.venv/` that I used for testing.",
  "final_message_truncated": false,
